## Roles
- Respect the separation of concerns between models, repositories, and business logic
- Use consistent error handling patterns
- When naming the package of files, use the form: "moduleName_(models, dtos, handler, ...)"
- When naming folders, use hyphens between words (e.g., plan-features)
- When naming a file, use - between words
- No need for seed data
- In BSON and JSON naming, use camelCase (e.g., bson:"isFilterable" json:"isFilterable")
- Make sure to follow function parameters and responses inside service repository declarations when implementing the base module
- Create a repository interface in the service to declare function types and return types
- Create an injector similar to other modules
- Follow the structure and core implementation similar to existing modules (like category) to maintain consistent application structure and declaration patterns
- Create Dto for create the model 
- if you need to use enums, put them inside an eums folder in the module
- Naming a file must be realted to our forms like; model file should be "modelName.model.go" same for repo "repoName.repo.go" also for dto, injector, enums, filter, handler, utils and service.
- In general when we creat new module we will need the following folders and files (dtos, enums, filters, handlers, models, repos, services) and an injector file.
- When you build the handler file, make sure to make it similer to form we use it in other modules.
- Dont naming ID name it like Id
- when naming and id use the form of Id instead of ID


